From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:45:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 018/342] dwc2: split transactions for low/full speed devices
 behind a hub

Keyboards and mice on the ODROID-C2 sit behind the onboard GL852G high
speed hub and need its transaction translator: one packet per
start-split (must be ACKed by the hub) and complete-split (retried each
microframe while NYET), toggles carried from packet to packet, a short
IN packet ends the transfer. As in FreeBSD's dwc_otg, interrupt
endpoints are issued as control type through the translator, so there is
no periodic complete-split window to hit; an interrupt NAK reschedules
the transfer.

The channel programming is shared with the high speed path
(_RunChannel). NOT YET TESTED on hardware: no low/full speed device was
plugged into the board. The high speed path (hub enumeration) was
re-tested after the refactoring.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
